  *** ENDF/B-VIII.0 Evaluation Documentation, January 2018 ***    9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The ENDF/B-VIII.0 evaluation comprises important modifications    9437 1451
from ENDF/B-VII.1 as described below for each section, in         9437 1451
increasing order of MF/MT.                                        9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF1, MT456,452 //                                              9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
Below 650 eV, the prompt and total nubar evaluation from the WPEC 9437 1451
Subgroup 34 [SG34] was adopted. Above 40 keV, the ENDF/B-VII.1    9437 1451
nubar values are used, but increased in the 0.3 to 1 MeV range for9437 1451
better performance in integral benchmarks. A more rigorous        9437 1451
analysis of the existing experimental database will be a high-    9437 1451
priority for the next release of the library.                     9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[SG34] Coordinated Evaluation of Plutonium-239 in the Resonance   9437 1451
Region, Coordinator: C. De Saint Jean, Monitor: R.D. McKnight,    9437 1451
NEA/NSC/WPEC/DOC(2014)447.                                        9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF1, MT458 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
An evaluation of the measured energy dependence of the post-      9437 1451
neutron emission average TKE has been performed by an adjustment  9437 1451
of some of the model parameters described in [Le14] based on exp- 9437 1451
erimental data for 239Pu from [Me16]. Average energy release for  9437 1451
prompt and delayed fission neutron and gamma emissions are derived9437 1451
data computed from the appropriate other sections. Other energy   9437 1451
release components should use the Sher and Beck systematics and   9437 1451
the thermal values as given.                                      9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Le14] Lestone and Strother, Energy dependence of plutonium and   9437 1451
uranium average fragment total kinetic energies, Nucl. Data       9437 1451
Sheets 118, 208 (2014).                                           9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Me16] Meierbachtol et al., Total kinetic energy release in       9437 1451
239Pu(n,f) post-neutron emission from 0.5 to 50 MeV incident      9437 1451
neutron energy, Phys. Rev. C 94, 34611 (2016).                    9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF2, MT151 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
Resolved resonance parameters imported from WPEC/SG34             9437 1451
(ORNL/CEA Cadarache).                                             9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
Unresolved resonance parameters are the same as ENDF/B-VI         9437 1451
evaluated by Derrien and Nakagawa (1993).                         9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF3, MT16 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
We slighlty increased the (n,2n) cross section near threshold,    9437 1451
and below 8 MeV, within the estimated one-sigma error bars of     9437 1451
the B-VII.1 values, based on the GEANIE experimental data. This   9437 1451
change was motivated by the seemingly unrealistic bent in the     9437 1451
cross section caused by only partial and limited experimental     9437 1451
information on the observation of the gamma decay chains. This    9437 1451
change was compensated by a slight decrease of the elastic        9437 1451
cross section in the corresponding energy range.                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF3, MT18 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The fission cross section above 40 keV and up to 20 MeV was       9437 1451
modified by adopting the final IAEA standard fission cross section9437 1451
evaluation released on Feb. 13, 2017 [Ca18]. This evaluation uses 9437 1451
a least-square fit (GMA code) of experimental data sets, including9437 1451
cross-isotope and cross-reaction correlations. The total cross    9437 1451
section was held constant by placing the small differences in the 9437 1451
elastic channel.                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ca18] A.D.Carlson et al., Estimation of the Neutron Data         9437 1451
Standards, to appear in the Special Issue of Nuclear Data Sheets  9437 1451
on ENDF/B-VIII and accompanying papers (2018).                    9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF3, MT102 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The capture cross section follows the recent modification of      9437 1451
ENDF/B-VII.1 above 30 keV to better match recent DANCE data by    9437 1451
Mosby et al. [Mo18] up to 0.7 MeV, where it switches to Kawano's  9437 1451
CoH3 calculations up to 20 MeV. A lin-log interpolation of the    9437 1451
calculated results was performed to keep the incident energy grid 9437 1451
unchanged. The modification of the capture cross section was      9437 1451
compensated by changes in the elastic channel to keep the total   9437 1451
cross section unchanged.                                          9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Mo18] S. Mosby et al., Plutonium capture DANCE experiment, to    9437 1451
appear in Nuclear Data Sheets (2018).                             9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF5, MT18 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The PFNS is given for incident neutron energies up to 20 MeV.     9437 1451
Different flavors of the Los Alamos model [Ma82] were used:       9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
*) The PFNS at thermal incident neutron energy was obtained by    9437 1451
slightly hardening the ENDF/B-VII.1 PFNS to achieve better        9437 1451
agreement of simulated neutron multiplication factors of selected 9437 1451
plutonium critical assemblies compared to their measured values.  9437 1451
The outgoing neutron energy range of the PFNS at thermal was      9437 1451
truncated to be maximally 20 MeV in correspondence with the       9437 1451
maximal incident neutron energy. The truncated PFNS was           9437 1451
renormalized such that the integral over the entire energy range  9437 1451
is unity.                                                         9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
*) The PFNS for incident neutron energies from 0.5 up to 5 MeV was9437 1451
carried over from ENDF/B-VII.1. Similarly to the thermal PFNS,    9437 1451
the PFNS data carried over from ENDF/B-VII.1 were truncated to an 9437 1451
outgoing neutron energy range of up to 20 MeV and re-normalized.  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
*) The PFNS data for incident neutron energies above 5 MeV were   9437 1451
obtained from a generalized least squares evaluation by Neudecker 9437 1451
et al. [Ne18] extending the original Los Alamos model to include  9437 1451
the effects of emission anisotropy and different fragment         9437 1451
temperatures, as well as to properly account for multi-chance     9437 1451
fission evaporation and  pre-equilibrium neutron spectra. This new9437 1451
 evaluation also includes recently published data by Lestone et   9437 1451
al. [Le14] and Chatillon et al. [Ch14] as well as recent findings 9437 1451
on possible biases in old measurements [Ta14,Ne16]. A detailed    9437 1451
uncertainty analysis was undertaken for model parameters and      9437 1451
experimental data.                                                9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
For all incident neutron energies, six data points were added to  9437 1451
the PFNS at the lowest outgoing neutron energies to better cover  9437 1451
the energy range from 1.0e-5 to 10 eV.                            9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ma82] D.G. Madland and J.R. Nix, "New Calculation of Prompt      9437 1451
Fission Neutron Spectra and Average Prompt Neutron                9437 1451
Multiplicities," Nucl. Sci. Eng. 81, 213-271 (1982).              9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ne18] D. Neudecker et al., "Evaluations of energy spectra of     9437 1451
neutrons emitted promptly in neutron-induced fission of 235U and  9437 1451
239Pu," Nucl. Data Sheets, to be published (2018).                9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Le14] J.P. Lestone and E.F. Shores, "Uranium and Plutonium       9437 1451
Average Prompt-fission Neutron Energy Spectra (PFNS) from the     9437 1451
Analysis of NTS NUEX Data," Nucl. Data Sheets 119, 213-216 (2014).9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ch14] A. Chatillon et al. , "Measurement of Prompt Neutron       9437 1451
Spectra from the 239Pu(n,f) Fission Reaction for Incident Neutron 9437 1451
Energies from 1 to 200 MeV," Phys. Rev. C 89, 014611 (2014).      9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ta14] T.N. Taddeucci et al. , "Multiple-scattering Corrections   9437 1451
to Measurements of the Prompt Fission Neutron Spectrum," Nucl.    9437 1451
Data Sheets 123, 135-139 (2015).                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ne16] D. Neudecker et al. , "The Need for Precise and Well-      9437 1451
documented Experimental Data on Prompt Fission Neutron Spectra    9437 1451
from Neutron-induced Fission of 239 Pu," Nucl. Data Sheets 131,   9437 1451
289-318 (2016).                                                   9437 1451
