// MF6, MT18 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The prompt fission neutron and gamma-ray multiplicity             9437 1451
probabilities have been included for the first time in ENDF/B.    9437 1451
The neutron evaluation is based on Terrell's formula, with model  9437 1451
parameters tuned to follow nu-bar and an evaluation by Zucker and 9437 1451
Holden [Zu] up to 10 MeV. The results are also close to Monte     9437 1451
Carlo Hauser-Feshbach (CGMF) calculations up to 20 MeV. The gamma 9437 1451
evaluation is based on CGMF simulations with the multiplicity     9437 1451
adjusted to reproduce the average multiplicity in file MF12/MT18. 9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Zu86] M.S.Zucker and N.E.Holden, Energy dependence of the neutron9437 1451
multiplicity in fast neutron induced fission of 235,238U and      9437 1451
239Pu, BNL-38491 (1986).                                          9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF12, MT18 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The prompt-gamma multiplicity was set to the experimental value   9437 1451
of Gatera [Ga17] at thermal neutron incident energy, and at higher9437 1451
incident energies was adjusted to reproduce the available total   9437 1451
gamma production data by Dake  [Dr70,Dr74] at several incident    9437 1451
neutron energies.                                                 9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ga17] Gatera et. al., Phys. Rev. C 95, 064609 (2017).            9437 1451
[Dr70] D.M.Drake, J.C.Hopkins, C.S.Young, and H.Conde, Nucl. Sci. 9437 1451
Eng. 40, 294 (1970)                                               9437 1451
[Dr74] D.M.Drake, Nucl. Sci. Eng. 55, 427 (1974)                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
