// MF 33 //                                                       9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The covariance matrices for all (n,xn), (n,g) and (n,f) reaction  9437 1451
channels were revisited for ENDF/B-VIII.0. However, no new        9437 1451
reaction model calculations were performed, and only limited      9437 1451
a posteriori adjustments were implemented to the cross section    9437 1451
covariance matrices present in ENDF/B-VII.1. For the PFNS howver, 9437 1451
new covariance matrices were evaluated for incident neutron       9437 1451
energies above the second-fission threshold, as described below.  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF31, MT452,456 //                                             9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The average prompt fission neutron multiplicity (nubar) covariance9437 1451
matrix was revisited conservatively to account for a rather large 9437 1451
spread of experimental data sets in the fast energy range. The    9437 1451
new standard for Cf252(sf) nubar uncertainty is 0.4%, which was   9437 1451
used as a threshold for Pu239 nubar uncertainties. A new thorough 9437 1451
evaluation of this quantity is a high-priority for the next       9437 1451
release of the library, including the estimation of its covariance9437 1451
matrix.                                                           9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT1 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The (n,tot) cross section was increased closer to 2%, instead of  9437 1451
~1% in the previous version, but the correlation matrix remains   9437 1451
unchanged.                                                        9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT2,4 //                                                 9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The elastic and inelastic covariance matrices are unchanged.      9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT16 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The (n,2n) cross section was slightly modified near threshold and 9437 1451
the uncertainties increased in the 10-15 MeV to better reflect the9437 1451
discrepancies and error bars in the reported experimental data in 9437 1451
this energy region.                                               9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT17 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The (n,3n) cross section and uncertainties are unchanged from     9437 1451
ENDF/B-VII.1                                                      9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT18 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The fission cross section uncertainties have been increased       9437 1451
substantially to follow the recommendations of the International  9437 1451
Standards group [Ca18] that introduced a 1.2% systematic and fully9437 1451
correlated component, based on an analysis of the spread of the   9437 1451
experimental data. A similar component was present in the         9437 1451
previous version, but only at the 0.4% level. This new component  9437 1451
dominates the relative standard deviations.                       9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ca18] A.D.Carlson et al., Estimation of the Neutron Data         9437 1451
Standards, to appear in the Special Issue of Nuclear Data Sheets  9437 1451
on ENDF/B-VIII and accompanying papers (2018).                    9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF33, MT102 //                                                 9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The capture cross section evaluation was revisited thanks to new  9437 1451
data by Mosby et al (2018) at DANCE up to ~1.2 MeV, and new model 9437 1451
calculations using the CoH3 code (Kawano, 2017). A new covariance 9437 1451
matrix was obtained, leading to a slight reduction of the         9437 1451
uncertainties below 1 MeV and an increase above 5 MeV.            9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF34, MT2 //                                                   9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
The JENDL4.0 covariance matrix was adopted.                       9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
// MF35, MT18 //                                                  9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
Four PFNS covariances are given spanning an incident neutron      9437 1451
energy range up to 20 MeV:                                        9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
*) For incident neutron energies up to 5 MeV, the ENDF/B-VII.1    9437 1451
covariance [Ta10] was carried over as also the data were carried  9437 1451
over. The incident neutron energy range was extended up to 5 MeV  9437 1451
(before 0.5 MeV) given that the underlying physics processes      9437 1451
(first chance fission) are similar and thus the covariances are   9437 1451
very similar for incident neutron energies below the second       9437 1451
chance fission threshold.                                         9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
*) For incident neutron energies above 5 MeV, the covariances     9437 1451
simultaneously evaluated with the data by Neudecker et al. [Ne18] 9437 1451
are provided. Covariances are given for incident neutron energy   9437 1451
bins spanning 5.0-6.5, 6.5-13.0, and 13.0-20 MeV corresponding to 9437 1451
the evaluation at incident neutron energies at 6, 10 and 14 MeV.  9437 1451
This binning was chosen as sampling from these covariances        9437 1451
produces on average the mean values and covariances closest to the9437 1451
original evaluated data and covariances considering covariances   9437 1451
for each incident neutron energy and cross-correlation between    9437 1451
them which cannot be stored in ENDF-6 format.                     9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ta10] P. Talou et al. , "Uncertainty Quantification of Prompt    9437 1451
Fission Neutron Spectrum for n(0.5 MeV)+ 239 Pu," Nucl. Sc. Eng.  9437 1451
166, 254-266 (2010).                                              9437 1451
                                                                  9437 1451
[Ne18] D. Neudecker et al., "Evaluations of energy spectra of     9437 1451
neutrons emitted promptly in neutron-induced fission of 235U and  9437 1451
239Pu," Nucl. Data Sheets, to be published (2018).                9437 1451
